X:1
T:Lord As To Thy Dear Cross
T:ST BERNARD RICHARDSON
C:Music: from Tochter Sion, Cologne, 1741 · Words: John Hampden Gurney, 1838
S:Open Hymnal Project ABC (openhymnal.org; marked public domain), melody line with every stanza as printed there; their source: "The New Hymnal (Episcopal)", 1916 Hymn 125 the oldest copy of this arrangement that I can find is in "Church Hymnal", 1877 hymn 345 attributed to W. Richardson. No second score was available to cross-check the melody.
