w: Lord, as to Thy dear * cross we flee, And plead to be for- giv'n,
w: Help us, through good re- * port and ill, Our dai- ly cross to bear:
w: Let grace our sel- fish- * ness ex- pel, Our earth- li- ness re- fine;
w: If joy shall at Thy * bid- ding fly, And grief's dark day come on,
w: Kept peace- ful in the * midst of strife, For- giv- ing and for- giv'n,
B | e c B c | A A G E | A G F F | E3|]
w: So let Thy life our pat- tern be, And form our souls for heav'n.
w: Like Thee, to do our Fa- ther's will, Our bre- thren's grief to share.
w: And kind- ness in our bo- soms dwell, As free and true as Thine.
w: We in our turn would meek- ly cry, "Fa- ther, Thy will be done."
w: O may we lead the pil- grim's life And fol- low Thee to heav'n.
